type: web_research
title: Claude Code permission whitelist research
key_insights[10]: "Anthropic official examples are minimal: settings-lax just disables bypass, settings-strict puts Bash on ask and denies WebSearch/WebFetch","Trail of Bits: NO allow list at all, only deny rules for credentials/secrets + hooks for rm -rf and push-to-main. Security-first approach.","thegeosman/claude-code-settings (900+ patterns): EXTREMELY permissive - allows rm -rf, curl, bash *, sh *, sudo *, docker exec rm, kill -9. Not a security model.",In default mode Read/Glob/Grep are auto-allowed. In plan mode everything needs explicit allow rules.,"Read, Edit, Write without parentheses = allow ALL uses. Read(**) with gitignore glob also works.","Edit/Write have built-in diff approval UX, so permission dialog is a double-prompt","Official docs warn curl patterns are fragile and recommending WebFetch(domain:) instead","MCP tool whitelisting is uncommon in community configs because most people use default mode, not plan mode",No community config whitelists osascript,call_tool_chain is effectively Bash(*) for MCP - executes arbitrary MCP calls
refs[5]: "https://code.claude.com/docs/en/permissions - Official permission docs","https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/tree/main/examples/settings - Official examples (lax, strict, bash-sandbox)","https://github.com/trailofbits/claude-code-config - Security-focused, deny-only approach","https://github.com/thegeosman/claude-code-settings - 900+ patterns, very permissive","https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/18160 - Known bug: Bash(ls *) not matching in global settings"
recommendations[7]: "Built-in tools (Read, Glob, Grep): universally safe, whitelist","Edit/Write: have built-in diff UX, safe to whitelist (no double-prompt)","Git/gh/tmux read-only: universally safe","MCP read-only tools: safe but uncommon in community (plan mode specific)","call_tool_chain and register_manual: NOT purely read-only, flag as power-user choice","praetorian_compact and gladiator_observe: append-only writes, flag as deliberate","Remove bash/sh/zsh/python3/curl from local: security holes confirmed by all sources"
